From: dArkOS RG52 Mini port
Subject: drm_go2 context on the RK3562 RG52 Mini: panel, colours, HDMI

Master rewrote this context (no libgo2: its own dumb buffers, the RGA blit
straight into them), for the Odroid Go Advance. What patches 0000, 0020 and
0025 did on v1.22.2's, done again on it:
- the RG52 Mini's portrait panel is mounted the other way round from the
  OGA's: the frame is turned by ROT_90, not ROT_270;
- 32-bit XRGB8888 scanout buffers, read by the RGA in the GL surface's own
  format: a copy with no conversion, so red and blue cannot swap on this
  RGA, and no RGB565 banding;
- the connector /var/run/drmConn names (the HDMI hotplug script writes it,
  as for SDL), else the first connected one;
- a landscape output (HDMI) is driven as it is, without a turn, where
  master refused it.

diff --git a/gfx/drivers_context/drm_go2_ctx.c b/gfx/drivers_context/drm_go2_ctx.c
index 6fe6069..2dfd4e9 100644
--- a/gfx/drivers_context/drm_go2_ctx.c
+++ b/gfx/drivers_context/drm_go2_ctx.c
